# Small rapid-fire cannon: cheap per shot, capacitor-hungry per second (18/s at full
# rate vs the gauss's 20/s but with far less alpha). Shines as a flak platform: 12
# shells/s of proximity screen. Shells are light and easy for enemy PD to burn.
id          autocannon_mk1
name        "Autocannon Mk I"
kind        ballistic
size        S
icon        ic-cannon
damage      6
fire_rate   12.0
proj_speed  10000
# Reach is proj_speed * proj_life, and proj_life IS the flight time to maximum reach. The
# whole ballistic catalog was scaled by 0.15 (14 -> 2.1s, 140,000 -> 21,000 units) so a shot
# lands in about two seconds instead of fourteen, and the engagement frames on screen. The
# factor is uniform across all four ballistics, so every authored balance relationship
# between them is unchanged -- this compresses range, it does not re-tune the catalog.
proj_life   2.1
proj_radius 3.0
cap_cost    1.5
emission    0.5
proj_hp     0.6
price       250
tier        1

# In-world turret art (446x688, barrels-up). Three barrels for the rapid-fire mount; see
# gauss_mk1 for what the size/pivot numbers mean.
mount_art       assets/weapons/assets/tier_1_cannon_triple_barrel.png
mount_art_size  1.95 3.00
mount_art_pivot -0.37

# Three barrels, measured off the art's alpha (cols 96..121 / 210..235 / 324..349 of 446,
# tips at row 5). SEQUENTIAL, so the authored 12 shells/s and 1.5 cap/shot are exactly what
# they were -- the barrels take turns rather than tripling the volley. At 12/s that is a
# barrel every 83 ms, which reads as all three working. A heavy triple-barrel that fires all
# three at once is `muzzle_pattern salvo`, but that is 3x the damage per capacitor charge and
# wants its own def and its own tuning, not a one-word edit here.
muzzle -0.50 1.85
muzzle  0.00 1.85
muzzle  0.50 1.85
muzzle_pattern sequential
desc "Cheap per shot, hungry per second. Its real trade is volume: a dozen light shells a second make the densest flak screen this side of tier two."
